# Everything here is machine-produced or machine-specific. The rule of thumb:
# if `git clean -xdf` would destroy a night of recordings, the directory belongs
# in /var (ignored, and never deleted by hand) rather than being merely untracked.

# --- Rust ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `**/` so a build run from inside a crate cannot leave a stray target/ behind.
**/target/
# rustfmt backup of a file it reformatted.
**/*.rs.bk
# MSVC debug symbols.
*.pdb
# `Cargo.lock` is NOT ignored on purpose: this workspace ships binaries, so the
# lockfile is the only record of the dependency set that was actually tested.

# --- Web (Vite + TypeScript) -----------------------------------------------
node_modules/
web/dist/
# `tsc -b` writes this next to the config on every type check. It is a stamp for
# incremental builds, not source, and it churns on every run.
*.tsbuildinfo
# Vite writes these while a dev server starts; a crash leaves them behind.
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# --- agent tool caches ------------------------------------------------------
# Per-task worktrees and clones. Regenerated on demand; never part of the tree.
.delta/

# --- Swift sidecar (apple-stt-sidecar) -------------------------------
# `build.sh` produces this and `install.sh` runs `build.sh` first, so a checkout
# does not need it. It is a compiled binary plus a signed bundle.
apple-stt-sidecar/build/
*.dSYM/

# --- Python tooling (tools/*.py) -------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# --- Local runtime state ---------------------------------------------------
# Written by tools/run-server.sh and tools/refresh-all.sh: config, the SQLite
# database, the recorded WAVs, the server log, the pid file. This is the real
# data of a real instance — off the index, and never deleted (tools/README.md).
/var/
# The same artifacts if a runtime directory is ever pointed inside the repo:
# SQLite and its WAL sidecars, an in-progress recording, the recogniser socket.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.wav.partial
*.sock
*.pid
*.log

# --- Local configuration ---------------------------------------------------
# The committed templates are `config.example.toml` (server) and
# `node.example.toml` (capture node). A real one names this machine's paths,
# device and LAN address.
/config.toml
/node.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
# AppleDouble resource forks, created on exFAT/USB volumes — the archive disk.
._*
.Spotlight-V100/
.Trashes/

# --- Editors ---------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Patch leftovers -------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej

# --- Test material ---------------------------------------------------------
# The steno-eval corpus is third-party audio, not source; it is fetched, not
# committed. Deploys are fine without it.
testdata/steno-eval/

# --- audio.cpp models ------------------------------------------------------
# `audiocpp_model_manager install <pkg>` writes packages under `$PWD/models`, so
# running it from the repo root leaves 1–4 GB of GGUF weights here. Weights are
# fetched per machine (`--backend audiocpp --model <dir>`), never committed.
/models/
